      "math_academy_id": "q-45448",
      "sequence_position": 5,
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14221743/assets/9fd4e55e5de09555b5a1fe05f8fb5f47b03d3b0cd9d96cbdca526f0d357d0afb.png)\n\nA stretch of factor $3$ in the $x$-direction and $2$ in the $y$-direction is applied to the polygon shown above. Which of the following is the resulting polygon?",
      "worked_solution": "A stretch of factor $3$ in the $x$-direction and $2$ in the $y$-direction can be represented by the following function:\n\n$$\n(x,y)↦(3x,2y)\n$$\n\nTo stretch a polygon, we \n\n- find the images of the vertices, and then\n\n- draw segments connecting the image vertices.\n\nSo, our three vertices $(1,3)$, $(1,-2)$, $(-2,2)$ are mapped to the following points by the stretch:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(1,3) & ↦(3\\cdot 1,2\\cdot 3)=(3,6) \\\\ (1,-2) & ↦(3\\cdot 1,2\\cdot (-2))=(3,-4) \\\\ (-2,2) & ↦(3\\cdot (-2),2\\cdot 2)=(-6,4)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain the following result:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14221743/assets/6c77ca7fa6efa27125c131c629b5afeba784b8ca4fd1039530879c2ec177b8dc.png)",
